{"id":"COR-18","class":"correctness","severity":"advisory","file":"src/ui/main.js","line":100,"what_breaks":"F-43 is closed for one of the two search boxes. Deleting a customer clears the customer search but not the order search. A name typed there to find that customer's orders stays in the Search orders box after the app has said all of this customer's data is erased, until a reload.","requirement":"R-04","evidence":"Type 'Ion' in Search orders: order-list.js:127 sets state.searchOrders = 'Ion'. Delete Ion's orders and then Ion. main.js:100 customerWasDeleted(nextData) is true but clears only state.searchCustomers. With any other customer's order left, renderOrderList takes buildList, and order-list.js:96 sets input.value = state.searchOrders, so 'Ion' is shown. R-10 searches customer name, so this box does hold names. eraseAll at main.js:181-182 clears both boxes, so the delete path is the odd one out.","proven":true},
{"id":"COR-19","class":"correctness","severity":"advisory","file":"src/domain/validation.js","line":7,"what_breaks":"Some invisible characters still count as text in a required field, so a customer or a line can be saved with nothing visible. A customer whose name is only U+034F then gets a list row link with no visible text to click.","requirement":"R-17","evidence":"INVISIBLE_ONLY is /^[\\p{Cf}\\p{Z}\\s]*$/u. U+034F combining grapheme joiner and U+FE0F variation selector are zero-width with category Mn. U+3164 and U+115F Hangul fillers are Lo. U+0001 is Cc. None is in Cf, Z or \\s, and String.trim keeps them. For name = U+034F, validation.js:43 test is false, length 1 passes the 1 to 100 check at :44, and validateCustomer returns ok. customer-list.js:32 then renders a link with no visible text. R-17 says zero-width or other format characters count as empty. tests/validation.test.js:186 and :193 use only Cf characters, so a stricter rule is untested. Severity is advisory because reaching it takes pasting an unusual code point and no data is lost.","proven":true},
